# tests/065-test-harness.lua

Shared helpers for the people-links tests.  `dofile` it; it returns a table
`H` holding counters `passed`, `failed` (integers) and these functions:

| function | takes | gives | purpose |
|---|---|---|---|
| `setup(dir, mode)` | string, `"stand-in"` or `"real"` | nothing | Loads the modules into `H.rooms`, `H.people`, `H.disk`, `H.names`, with the stand-in room-folders (064) or the real one.  Errors on another mode, or on `real` before 101's file exists. |
| `module_present(relative)` | string | bool | Whether a file under the project exists (for neighbour tests). |
| `fresh_home(name, collision, own_devices, split_records)` | string ×4 (last two optional: `"none"`, `"show"`) | home | A new rao-home under `tmp/shared-memory/people-links/<mode>-<name>`, config set, contacts written (girlfriend, friend, housemate, and an own device `phone`). |
| `room(home, name, parent_id, recipients)` | home, string, string, list of string | string room id | Shorthand for `create_room`. |
| `view(home, contact)` | home, string or nil | list of string, sorted | Everything under `people/` (or one person's folder): `"path -> target"` for links, `"path/"` for folders, `"path (file)"` for files. |
| `check(ok, label)` / `same(got, want, label)` / `fails(fn, fragment, label)` | | nothing | Count a check; `same` compares lists of strings; `fails` wants an error containing `fragment`. |
| `list_has(list, wanted)` | list, value | bool | Membership. |
| `link_to(contact, name, room_id)` | strings | string | An expected view line for a flat link. |
| `finish()` | — | exits | Prints `RESULT <mode> pass=N fail=M`, exits non-zero on any failure. |
